>      * Should not be possible to tin rust monsters.

Tins in nethack are made of METAL which is not rustable or corrodeable
according to the normal "physics". Your tinning kit however is made of
IRON, as is your tin opener. I've written a patch [1] which makes
tinning any monster with a rust or corrode or opening such a tin attack
will have the corresponding effects on your tools (or weapons, if you
use a dagger to open the tin).

[1] http://www.cse.unsw.edu.au/~malcolmr/nethack/3.4.3/rusty-tins.diff

I've also changed the code so that rusty tools take longer to use and
enchanted tools take less time.
This was a bit involved as I had to change tinning so it took more than
one turn, and I had to handle the possibility that the corpse might rot
away while you were trying to tin it.

I haven't tested it very thoroughly yet. Let me know if you have any
problems.

